[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Third Reference Slice - Reproducible Variation Campaigns

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Iterations 101-150 add bounded immutable scalar variations and evidence improvements to the reference engine. They do not claim distributed execution, hostile-input sandboxing, nonlinear device qualification, or a production StressForge integration.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF3-001
TITLE: Immutable scalar variation
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference engine shall derive scalar component variations by cloning and validating the public circuit representation, without mutating compiled plans or changing the base circuit.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/variation.rs.
Verification: tests/variation.rs::replacement_is_immutable_and_validated.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF2-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF3-002
TITLE: Bounded deterministic variation products
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference engine shall validate bounded scalar sweep and grid inputs, retain caller declared dimension/value ordering, and give every generated point a stable indexed case identity.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/variation.rs, src/sweep.rs.
Verification: tests/variation.rs::sweep_preserves_declared_order_and_rejects_unbounded_input, tests/variation.rs::grid_has_deterministic_cartesian_order.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF2-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF3-003
TITLE: Point-isolated variation execution
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference engine shall report a success or failure for each completed variation point and only observe cooperative cancellation between points.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/sweep.rs.
Verification: tests/variation.rs::scalar_sweep_returns_stable_indexed_cases, tests/variation.rs::cancellation_is_observed_between_sweep_points.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF2-008
